<title>CANADA: Ault churns higher on sale, raised buyback.</title>
<headline>Ault churns higher on sale, raised buyback.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ault Foods Ltd stock rose in early trading on Friday, boosted by the long-awaited news that it was selling its fluid milk assets and raising its share buyback plan to C$180 million from C$100 million.</p>
<p>&quot;That was certainly postive, more shares being bought back,&quot; said Deacon Capital analyst Bill Chisholm.</p>
<p>Shares in the dairy firm jumped as much as 1.00 to 23.00 but settled back to 22.25, a gain of 0.50, in active dealings on the Toronto Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Ault said it would sell its fluid milk operations and cottage cheese, sour cream manufacturing and other assets to Agropur agri-food cooperative for about C$145 million.</p>
<p>Chisholm added Ault's stock, which traded around 18.60 in early January, had been driven higher in recent weeks on expectations of the sale.</p>
<p>((Lydia Zajc, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
